After several iteration with  @ktl  and  @rowen  we finally solved this. The Swig interface should contain: 
 %include "lsst/meas/simastrom/CountedRef.h"
%template(CcdImageCountedRef) lsst::meas::simastrom::CountedRef ;
%template(CcdImageCountedRefList) std::list  >;
%include "lsst/meas/simastrom/CcdImage.h"

 In this order. The bottom line is that Swig is processing the .i file in one single pass, so every ÒobjectÓ should be known before being used.

